  "details": "I wanted to provide feedback on the new ik improvements, I tested the delay with a friend of mine, my ping was around 220-230, his was 200. as for movement delays, it has improved a lot compared to the live version, there's only under a second delay that doesn't hinder interactions that much, but still needs a bit of work.\nas for objects sync, it's still bad and the delay is larger than the movement. there's still a two seconds delay for example when one player throws an object and the other one grabs it, it falls to the ground, stays there for a bit and then teleports to the player's hand. it's still better than it is in live (2 instead of 4 seconds delay).\nFor clarification, despite our medium/high ping, being in eu, the old ik didn't have these problems, movement delay wasn't noticeable, and object sync was perfect, there was only a delay between action and voice, but that's just cause of the high ping.\nthe two logs:\n220-240 ping:\nhttps://gist.github.com/lucabesa/b64ddb04bce8bb497f2739f14226858c\n200 ping:\nhttps://gist.github.com/lucabesa/e99c807310373bddea618db8b936954e",
